# fifo_gap_barrier_signed_distance: Barriers compare (int32_t)(slot - value) >= 0, so they wrap: with root slot 0 at 0xfffffffe, a barrier on value 0x7fffffff (distance 2^31 - 1) passes at once, while one on 0x7ffffffe (distance 2^31, negative) blocks child 1 (a 300 ms wait that times out is the behaviour). Root stamps 2 and 0x7ffffffd leave it blocked; 0x7ffffffe releases it. A barrier on 5 while the slot reads 0xfffffffb blocks until the stamp wraps through 0 to 5.
